<article class="env-corollary" id="05FQ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05FQ">Corollary <span data-tag="05FQ">4.7.2.14</span> <span class="named">(Composition)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category containing a $2$-simplex </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  Y \ar [dr]^{ g } &amp;  \\ X \ar [ur]^{f} \ar [rr]^{h} &amp;  &amp;  Z, } \]
</div>
<p> and let $n$ be an integer. Then: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
If the morphisms $f$ and $g$ are $n$-truncated, then the morphism $h$ is $n$-truncated. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
If the morphism $h$ is $n$-truncated and the morphism $g$ is $(n+1)$-truncated, then the morphism $f$ is $n$-truncated. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Proposition <a data-tag="05FM" href="/tag/05FM">4.7.2.11</a> to the slice $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/Z}$ (see Proposition <a data-tag="05FF" href="/tag/05FF">4.7.2.7</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
